1 0 0 1 56 770 Tm (# Moving off server-side sessions) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 756 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 56 742 Tm (We spent most of last week on the load test results and the picture was pretty clear.) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 728 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 56 714 Tm (The session store was the bottleneck. Once we got past roughly 400 requests per second, the) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 700 Tm (lookup on every single request started queueing and p99 latency went from 40ms to well over) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 686 Tm (a second. Adding read replicas helped a bit but it moved the problem rather than solving it) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 672 Tm (— we were still doing a network round trip per request just to find out who the caller was.) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 658 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 56 644 Tm (So we're dropping server-side sessions and going with stateless JWT. The token carries the) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 630 Tm (claims we actually need, we verify the signature locally, and there's no lookup at all on) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 616 Tm (the hot path. Refresh tokens stay server-side because we need to be able to revoke them, but) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 602 Tm (those are touched maybe once an hour per user rather than on every request.) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 588 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 56 574 Tm (The tradeoff we're accepting is that we can't invalidate an access token before it expires.) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 560 Tm (We're setting the access token TTL to 15 minutes to keep that window small.) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 546 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 56 532 Tm (— Basuru, 2026-05-14) Tj
1 0 0 1 56 518 Tm () Tj
